```

## Scroller Architecture

The app uses a unified, modular scroller system with two levels of abstraction:

### Component Hierarchy

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ useScrollDrag (Hook) - src/hooks/use-scroll-drag.ts         │
│  - Drag-to-scroll with 5px threshold (fixes click vs drag)  │
│  - Arrow scroll function (80% of visible width)             │
│  - External ref support for forwardRef components           │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                              │
                              ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ ScrollContainer (Primitive) - media/scroll-container.tsx    │
│  - Low-level scrollable container                           │
│  - Drag-to-scroll + optional arrow controls                 │
│  - ForwardRef support for external scroll control           │
│  - Use for custom scroll UIs (image galleries, video lists) │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                              │
                              ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ MediaScroller (Composite) - media/media-scroller.tsx        │
│  - High-level scroller section with header                  │
│  - Title, icon, "See All" link, arrow controls in header    │
│  - Uses ScrollContainer internally                          │
│  - Use for standard content sections (cast, recs, etc.)     │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### useScrollDrag Hook

The foundation hook that handles drag-to-scroll with click detection:

```typescript
import { useScrollDrag } from "@/hooks/use-scroll-drag";

function MyScroller() {
  const {
    scrollRef,           // Ref to attach to scroll container
    setScrollRef,        // Callback ref (for forwardRef)
    isDragging,          // Whether actively dragging
    handlePointerDown,   // Pointer event handlers
    handlePointerMove,
    handlePointerUp,
    handleDragStart,     // Prevents native drag
    scroll,              // (direction: "left" | "right") => void
  } = useScrollDrag({ scrollAmount: 0.8 });
}
```

**Key feature:** 5px drag threshold - movement below this is treated as a click, allowing normal navigation. Pointer capture only activates AFTER threshold is exceeded.

**Mobile touch behavior:**
- Use `touch-manipulation` CSS (NOT `touch-pan-x`) on scroll containers
- `touch-pan-x` blocks vertical page scrolling when touch starts on a scroller
- `touch-manipulation` allows both horizontal scroll on the scroller AND vertical page scroll

### ScrollContainer Component

Low-level scrollable container for custom UIs:

```tsx
import { ScrollContainer } from "@/components/features/media";

// Basic usage
<ScrollContainer gap="gap-3" padding="px-4">
  {items.map(item => <Card key={item.id} />)}
</ScrollContainer>

// With arrow controls at edge (default)
<ScrollContainer showControls gap="gap-4" padding="px-4 md:px-8">
  {items}
</ScrollContainer>

// Without controls (for custom UIs like image galleries)
<ScrollContainer showControls={false}>
  {images}
</ScrollContainer>
```

**Props:**
- `showControls` - Show arrow buttons (default: true)
- `controlsPosition` - "edge" (default) or "inline"
- `gap` - Tailwind gap class (default: "gap-4")
- `padding` - Tailwind padding class (default: none)
- `bottomPadding` - Bottom padding (default: "pb-4")

### MediaScroller Component

High-level scroller for content sections:

```tsx
import { MediaScroller } from "@/components/features/media";
import { Users } from "lucide-react";

<MediaScroller
  title="Top Cast"
  titleIcon={<Users className="h-5 w-5 text-brand" />}
  seeAllHref="/browse?cast=500"
  seeAllLabel="Browse All"
  contentPadding="px-4 md:px-8 lg:px-12"
  gap="gap-4"
>
  {cast.map(member => <PersonCard key={member.id} person={member} />)}
</MediaScroller>
```

**Props:**
- `title` - Section title (ReactNode)
- `titleIcon` - Icon before title
- `seeAllHref` - URL for "View All" link
- `seeAllLabel` - Custom link text (default: "View All")
- `contentPadding` - Padding for header and scroll area (default: "px-4 md:px-8 lg:px-12")
- `gap` - Gap between items (default: "gap-4")
- `showControls` - Show arrow controls (default: true)

### Which Scroller to Use

| Use Case | Component |
|----------|-----------|
| **Content sections** (cast, recommendations, collection) | `MediaScroller` |
| **Custom layouts** (image gallery, video sidebar) | `ScrollContainer` |
| **Infinite scroll** (discover scroller) | `useScrollDrag` hook directly |

