## Homepage Sections

### Personalized Sections (Split Components)

`ContinueWatchingSection` and `RecentVisitsSection` are separate components for flexible positioning:

```tsx
// src/components/features/home/personalized-sections.tsx
"use client";

export function ContinueWatchingSection() {
  const { status } = useSafeSession();
  const isHydrated = useUserStore(selectIsHydrated);
  const continueWatching = useUserStore(selectContinueWatching);

  if (status !== "authenticated") return null;
  if (!isHydrated) return <WideCarousel loading ... />;
  if (continueWatching.length === 0) return null;

  return <WideCarousel title="Continue Watching" items={continueWatching} showWatchLinks />;
}

export function RecentVisitsSection() {
  const { status } = useSafeSession();
  const isHydrated = useUserStore(selectIsHydrated);
  const recents = useUserStore(selectRecents);

  if (status !== "authenticated") return null;
  if (!isHydrated || recents.length === 0) return null;

  return <WideCarousel title="Recent Visits" items={recents} />;
}
```

### TrailerCarousel Component

Displays trending movie trailers with YouTube metadata:

```tsx
// src/components/features/home/trailer-carousel.tsx
interface TrendingTrailer {
  tmdbId: number;
  title: string;
  mediaType: "movie";  // TV series skipped (TMDB has stale Season 1 trailers)
  youtubeKey: string;
  trailerType: string; // "Trailer" | "Teaser"
  // ... other fields
}

// Features:
// - YouTube thumbnail with hover play button
// - Trailer/Teaser type badge
// - Movie title linked to detail page
// - YouTube stats (views + like/dislike ratio bar)
// - Click to play in TrailerModal

// YouTube metadata fetched client-side:
useEffect(() => {
  fetch(`/api/youtube?videoIds=${videoIds}`)
    .then(/* set videoMetadata state */);
}, [trailers]);
```

**Data source:** `getTrendingTrailers()` combines:
- Trending movies (currently popular)
- Upcoming movies (trailers being promoted)
- Now playing movies (fresh releases)

### TrailerModal Component

Full-featured trailer modal using shadcn Dialog. Used by both `TrailerCarousel` (TMDB) and `YouTubeTrailerCarousel` (YouTube channels), as well as the detail page play button.

```tsx
// src/components/features/home/trailer-modal.tsx
interface TrailerModalData {
  youtubeKey: string;
  title: string;           // Movie/show title
  trailerTitle: string;    // Full trailer title from YouTube
  tmdbId?: number;         // Optional - links to detail page
  mediaType?: "movie" | "tv";
  publishedAt?: string;
  channelTitle?: string;
  // Stats (loaded client-side)
  viewCount?: number;
  likeCount?: number;
  dislikeCount?: number;
}

interface TrailerModalProps {
  trailers: TrailerModalData[];
  currentIndex: number;
  isOpen: boolean;
  onClose: () => void;
  onNavigate: (index: number) => void;  // For prev/next
}
```

**Features:**
- **Proper Dialog** - Uses shadcn Dialog (ESC to close, backdrop, animations)
- **Large size** - Nearly full screen (`95vh`, `max-w-[1600px]`)
- **Two-column layout** (desktop) - Video + metadata on left, comments on right
- **Video metadata** - Title, views, date, like/dislike ratio bar
- **Video description** - Collapsible, auto-links URLs
- **Prev/Next navigation** - Shows trailer titles, keyboard arrows work
- **Comments section** - Scrollable list, shows total count from YouTube
- **Watch on YouTube button** - Red branded button

**Used by:**
- `TrailerCarousel` - Homepage TMDB trailers
- `YouTubeTrailerCarousel` - Homepage viral trailers from YouTube channels
- `MediaActionBar` - Detail page "Play Trailer" button (single trailer)

### Homepage Order

```tsx
// src/app/page.tsx
<div className="px-4 md:px-8 lg:px-12 pb-16 space-y-10">
